// M3 field-report corpus wave 3 (PLAN-D10, finding 3). Same geometry and wire ids as
// repeater_loop_clock_delay1_pulse1.ron (that file's own header has the full re-derivation) —
// repeaters here are delay=4 instead of delay=1, driven by a 10-game-tick, button-scale pulse.
ContraptionSpec(
    id: "redstone/clock/repeater_loop_clock_delay4_button_pulse",
    category: Clock,
    description: "Two opposing delay=4 repeaters joined by two 2-wire chains (an L-turn each way) — same loop-clock topology as repeater_loop_clock_delay1_pulse1.ron, scaled to the maximum DELAY setting — kick-started by a 10-game-tick, button-scale pulse.",
    quirk: "A 10-tick pulse is longer than a single delay=4 repeater's own 8-tick delay window, which is the actual threshold for permanent lock-on in this loop topology (not the loop's full 16-tick period) — the same turn-on-without-reschedule mechanism as the delay=1 long-pulse case, just on a longer timescale (M3 field-report wave 3 finding 3, 08-redstone-ticking.md §3.6).",
    max_ticks: 60,
